(HK DSE Biology — Photosynthesis \(detailed test notes\)) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(1. Overview) Tj T*
(Photosynthesis converts light energy into chemical energy in green plants,) Tj T*
(algae, and some bacteria. Carbon dioxide and water become glucose and oxygen.) Tj T*
(Word equation: carbon dioxide + water -> glucose + oxygen \(light, chlorophyll\).) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(2. Where it happens) Tj T*
(Leaf palisade cells are packed with chloroplasts. Chlorophyll a and b in the) Tj T*
(thylakoid membranes absorb red and blue light and reflect green.) Tj T*
(Stomata on the lower epidermis let CO2 in and O2 and water vapour out.) Tj T*
(Xylem brings water from roots. Phloem exports sugars as sucrose.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(3. Light-dependent stage \(thylakoid / grana\)) Tj T*
(Photolysis splits water: 2 H2O -> 4H+ + 4e- + O2. Electrons enter photosystem II,) Tj T*
(then photosystem I. NADP+ is reduced to NADPH. ATP is made by chemiosmosis) Tj T*
(through ATP synthase \(photophosphorylation\). Oxygen diffuses out via stomata.) Tj T*
ET
endstream
