7 0 obj<< /Length 1047 >>stream
BT /F1 11 Tf 56 740 Td 14 TL
(4. Light-independent stage \(Calvin cycle, stroma\)) Tj T*
(Rubisco fixes CO2 onto ribulose bisphosphate \(RuBP\). The product is reduced) Tj T*
(using ATP and NADPH to triose phosphate. Some triose becomes glucose;) Tj T*
(the rest regenerates RuBP. Temperature, CO2 concentration, and light) Tj T*
(intensity can each limit the rate \(limiting factors\).) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(5. Limiting factors \(exam points\)) Tj T*
(- Low light: fewer electrons and less ATP/NADPH, so Calvin cycle slows.) Tj T*
(- Low CO2: rubisco has less substrate; extra light cannot raise the rate.) Tj T*
(- Low temperature: enzyme \(rubisco\) collisions slow; rate falls.) Tj T*
(A graph of rate vs light rises then plateaus when CO2 or temperature limits.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(6. Adaptations of the leaf) Tj T*
(Broad lamina captures light. Thin blade shortens the diffusion path.) Tj T*
(Waxy cuticle cuts water loss. Air spaces in the spongy mesophyll hold CO2.) Tj T*
(Guard cells open stomata in light when photosynthesis uses CO2.) Tj T*
ET
endstream
