(7. Compare respiration) Tj T*
(Photosynthesis stores energy; aerobic respiration in mitochondria releases it.) Tj T*
(In light, net gas exchange is O2 out and CO2 in. In the dark, only respiration.) Tj T*
(Compensation point: photosynthesis rate equals respiration rate.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(8. Common DSE mistakes) Tj T*
(Chlorophyll does not 'make' food by itself; it captures light for the reactions.) Tj T*
(Oxygen comes from water photolysis, not from carbon dioxide.) Tj T*
(Glucose is often converted to starch for storage or sucrose for transport.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(9. Quick check) Tj T*
(Name the two stages, the organelle, the pigment, the gas in, the gas out,) Tj T*
(and one limiting factor. Explain why a brightly lit sealed tube of pondweed) Tj T*
(produces bubbles faster when sodium hydrogencarbonate is added \(more CO2\).) Tj T*
ET
